    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Only `AcceptanceTest` exists (one test, `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity`), and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` field so it returns `true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349** owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the hard rejection at 50 unchanged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `capacityWarning` boolean (read-only) to the `OwnerDto` schema, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` field. The generator produces the DTO field at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ...)` and a `capacityWarning(Owner)` method. It counts owners in the same city (excluding the owner itself), using the same case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsing normalization as `EnsureCityCapacity`, and returns `true` when the count is `>= 40 && < 50`. I introduced `CITY_CAPACITY_LIMIT` (50) and `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (40) constants to keep the boundary explicit and consistent with the hard-limit check.\n\nThe hard rejection path (`EnsureCityCapacity` throwing `CityAtCapacityException` at 50) was left untouched. The warning boundary aligns with it: the 50th successful create (49 others) still warns, while the 51st is rejected before responding.",
